Give the phone its own composition

The site was not broken on a phone so much as unaware of one. Every layout
decision — the book beside the copy, letters projected onto page rectangles,
a pinned horizontal gallery, a transparent nav floating over inset content —
only holds above roughly 1000px wide, and the old max-width:760px block shrank
those decisions rather than replacing them. Letter body text computed to
11.5px inside a scroll box nested in a pinned, Lenis-driven section.

Below 760px:

- Letters open full-screen in #letterSheet at 16px/1.78 over a 34-48ch
  measure. The views are MOVED into the sheet rather than cloned, so the
  voice-note card keeps its listener and the copy stays a single source of
  truth for i18n; closeLetterSheet() returns each node to its recorded parent
  and sibling. All of a letter's spreads are placed at once, and "Turn to the
  page" reveals the excerpt in place instead of running the 3D page turn.
- The nav is 3.5rem, clears the safe-area inset, and frosts once scrolled.
  Previously it was 108px, transparent, and full-width copy collided with it
  in every section.
- The hero book is large enough to read as a book (was ~90px at 0.23 scale)
  and sits clear of both the nav and the headline.
- The open sequence is +=170% rather than +=260%, with the question arriving
  at 0.42 — the old timing held a blank spread for over a viewport, since
  nothing is printed on those pages here.
- Movements is a native snap carousel with progress dots; the pinned
  horizontal ScrollTrigger is skipped.
- Sections measure in svh, not vh, so a collapsing address bar neither hides
  content nor churns ScrollTrigger.
- setPixelRatio caps at 1.5; a 390px canvas at DPR 3 was rendering 780x1328.
- Every a/button is at least 44px tall. viewport-fit=cover and safe-area
  insets throughout.

Desktop composition is unchanged — verified at 1440x900: the projection still
positions the pages, both pins still build, no dots injected.

Measured at 390x664: letter body 11.5px -> 16px, tap targets under 44px
20+ -> 0, page height 9,938px -> 8,735px, pinned sections 2 -> 1.

MOBILE.md carries the full audit and what is still open. CLAUDE.md is new:
ground rules for working in here.
